<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia CN Asia Corp debuts at 5.00 rgt.</title>
<headline>Malaysia CN Asia Corp debuts at 5.00 rgt.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of engineering firm CN Asia Corporation Bhd made their debut on the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange (KLSE) at 5.00 ringgit each against an offer price of 1.90.</p>
<p>The company had offered for public subscription 4.365 million new shares and 1.035 million existing shares at 1.90 ringgit.  </p>
<p>The company has forecast a net profit of 4.24 million ringgit in 1997 on an equity of 36 million shares of one ringgit each. At the issue price, the net price-to-earnings ratio works out to 16.13 times for 1997.</p>
<p>At its opening price, the PE ratio works out to around 42.44, brokers said.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-201 4813)</p>
